#
# Opengrep/semgrep path exclusions.
#
# examples/ are adopter-facing documentation snippets, not executed
# workflows. They pass each secret by name in an explicit `secrets:`
# mapping, matching the secrets each orchestrator declares at the
# workflow_call boundary.
examples/

# Go test files. The flagged patterns are the point of the tests, not
# attack surfaces: PGP/JWT-shaped fixtures feeding redaction and
# gpg-import tests, direct writes to httptest ResponseWriters in
# protocol mocks, exec.Command of freshly built test binaries, and
# reflect-by-name in table-driven key tests.
*_test.go

# Test helpers and the live harness that only tests and the operator run:
# they exec the tools a test selects, read capped archives, and check API
# responses for nil before use, the same reasons as for the test files.
internal/testutil/
test/live/internal/

# Live trial fixtures are test inputs. Adapter workflows carry ENGINE_SHA,
# which prepare.sh replaces with the full engine commit, and the Android
# app's launcher activity must be exported for the platform to start it.
test/live/fixtures/

# Live workflow fixtures pin PIN_FORGE_CI_SHA, which Layer.Render replaces
# with the exact served commit and refuses if any placeholder survives.
# They are test inputs, not workflows a forge can run as committed.
test/live/conformance/testdata/layer/
